.policy "postgres-migrations-practice-column-type-change-rewrites" revision 1
.description "Don't change a column's type on a table earlier migrations created unless the change is a no-rewrite widening: PostgreSQL rewrites the table and its indexes under an ACCESS EXCLUSIVE lock."
.language sql
.mode steer
.scope include "**/migrations/**/*.sql", "**/drizzle/**/*.sql", "**/migrations/migration_lock.toml"
.scope text "**/migrations/migration_lock.toml"
.scope exclude "**/node_modules/**", "**/.next/**", "**/dist/**", "**/build/**", "**/out/**", "**/coverage/**", "**/__tests__/**", "**/__mocks__/**", "**/test/**", "**/tests/**", "**/fixtures/**", "**/*.test.*", "**/*.spec.*"
// Rerail's own rule, not a port. `ALTER TABLE t ALTER COLUMN c [SET DATA] TYPE …` rewrites the whole table and every
// index on it while it holds ACCESS EXCLUSIVE (no reads, no writes), unless the old type is binary coercible to the
// new one and no USING changes the values. On a large table that is an outage for the length of the rewrite.
// The old type is the column's latest earlier definition among the migrations of the same migrations directory
// (CREATE TABLE, ADD COLUMN or an earlier TYPE change), ordered by migration name (lib/postgres-migrations' pgm_mig:
// Prisma's `YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_` folder, drizzle's `NNNN_` file), then by position in the file. A table is named by its
// last part, folded as PostgreSQL does.
// Reports, at the ALTER COLUMN:
//   ALTER COLUMN "count" SET DATA TYPE BIGINT                  INTEGER before: int → bigint rewrites
//   ALTER COLUMN "state" TYPE "State_new" USING (…::text::…)   Prisma's enum change: USING recasts every row
//   ALTER COLUMN "title" SET DATA TYPE VARCHAR(50)             TEXT or VARCHAR(100) before: shrinking or adding a limit
//   ALTER COLUMN "amount" SET DATA TYPE DECIMAL(10,4)          DECIMAL(10,2) before: a new scale rewrites
//   ALTER COLUMN "role" TYPE "Role" USING "role"::"Role"       old type unknown (dropped, renamed, squashed): a USING
//                                                              means no assignment cast exists, so values are converted
// Leaves alone:
//   a table created or emptied earlier in the same file, or given a NOT NULL column with no default before it
//   (pgm_fresh_table: it is empty; Prisma's init migration, a new table and its follow-ups)
//   VARCHAR(n) → VARCHAR(m ≥ n), VARCHAR(n) → VARCHAR or TEXT, NUMERIC(p,s) → NUMERIC(q ≥ p,s) or NUMERIC,
//   TIMESTAMP(p) → TIMESTAMP(q ≥ p) and the same for TIMESTAMPTZ, TIME, INTERVAL, VARBIT: binary coercible, no rewrite
//   TIMESTAMP → TIMESTAMPTZ and TIMESTAMPTZ → TIMESTAMP: no rewrite on PostgreSQL 12+ when the session's TimeZone is
//   UTC (it may be; not known here), so both directions are left alone alike
//   TEXT or VARCHAR → CITEXT and back: the citext extension's casts are binary (indexes on the column are still rebuilt)
//   the same type again, with no USING or a USING that casts the column once (`USING "x"::TEXT` on a TEXT column)
//   a column whose old type no earlier migration of its directory shows (squashed or baselined history), without USING
//   a migration that is not pending (pgm_pending: with a Git base, one the base has; without one, any but the newest
//   of its directory), or another database's
//   a column dropped or renamed (DROP COLUMN, RENAME COLUMN) since its last definition, without USING: type unknown
// Gaps: a renamed column or table is not followed back to its old definition (unknown, so reported only with USING);
// a USING that keeps the values (`USING "x"::TEXT` on a TEXT column) is reported when the old type is unknown;
// a schema-qualified table is matched by its last name part only; `TIMESTAMPTZ(3)` loses its precision in the
// grammar, so a precision decrease on it reads as a removal (not reported); a domain over the new type is reported;
// a table's size is unknown, so a small lookup table is reported too (the message says when to keep the change);
// a table created by an earlier migration that is still pending with this one is empty, which only a Git base shows.

#include "lib/postgres-migrations.rerail"

.violation ColumnTypeChangeRewrites(at: node, col: symbol, tbl: symbol, from: symbol, to: symbol) "Changing \"{col}\" on \"{tbl}\" from {from} to {to} rewrites the whole table and its indexes under an ACCESS EXCLUSIVE lock, blocking every read and write until it finishes. On a table with real data, add a new column of the new type, write both columns from the app, backfill the new one in batches, then switch reads and drop the old column in later migrations; when this recreates an enum only to drop a value, keep the value in the enum and stop using it instead. If the table is small or not yet in use in production, this migration is fine as it is."
ColumnTypeChangeRewrites(a, x, t, f, n) :- ctc_alter(a, d, t, x), ctc_old(a, od), ctc_desc(a, n), ctc_rewrites(a, od),
    ctc_existing(a, d), ctc_desc(od, o), (o != n, f = o ; o = n, f = "its old type").
// With the old type unknown, any USING counts: PostgreSQL asks for one only when no assignment cast converts the values.
ColumnTypeChangeRewrites(a, x, t, "its old type", n) :- ctc_alter(a, d, t, x), !ctc_old(a, _), ctc_using_expr(a, _),
    ctc_desc(a, n), ctc_existing(a, d).
// ctc_existing(a, d): a's migration d is pending and a's table may hold rows.
.decl ctc_existing(a: node, d: number)
ctc_existing(a, d) :- ctc_alter(a, d, t, _), child(s, a, _), !pgm_fresh_table(s, t), pgm_pending(d).

// ---- order: a node's place in its migrations directory --------------------------------------------------------------
// ctc_pos(n, root, m, off): node n stands at byte off of migration m of root.
.decl ctc_pos(n: node, root: symbol, m: symbol, off: number)
ctc_pos(n, r, m, o) :- ctc_at(n), docof(n, d), pgm_mig(d, r, m), node(d, n, _, o, _).
.decl ctc_at(n: node)
ctc_at(n) :- ctc_def(n, _, _).
ctc_at(n) :- ctc_reset(n, _, _).
// ctc_before(a, b): b runs before a in the same migrations directory.
.decl ctc_before(a: node, b: node)
ctc_before(a, b) :- ctc_alter(a, _, t, x), ctc_def(b, t, x), ctc_pos(a, r, ma, oa), ctc_pos(b, r, mb, ob),
    (mb < ma ; mb = ma, ob < oa).

// ---- column definitions ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Tables are lib's pgm_target (folded, the last name part), columns its pgm_ident.
// ctc_def(p, t, x): p gives column x of table t a type: a column definition (CREATE TABLE, ADD COLUMN) or a TYPE change.
.decl ctc_def(p: node, t: symbol, x: symbol)
ctc_def(p, t, x) :- kind(p, "column_definition"), (within(p, s), kind(s, "create_table") ; within(p, s), kind(s, "alter_table")),
    pgm_target(s, t), field(p, "name", n), pgm_ident(n, x).
ctc_def(a, t, x) :- ctc_alter(a, _, t, x).
// ctc_alter(a, d, t, x): ALTER COLUMN x [SET DATA] TYPE … on table t, in document d, outside a function body.
.decl ctc_alter(a: node, d: number, t: symbol, x: symbol)
ctc_alter(a, d, t, x) :- kind(a, "alter_column"), child(a, k, _), kind(k, "keyword_type"), child(s, a, _),
    kind(s, "alter_table"), pgm_target(s, t), field(a, "name", n), pgm_ident(n, x), docof(a, d), !routine_body(a).
// ctc_using(a): a has a USING clause that may change the values: anything but the column itself or one cast of it
// (`USING "x"::TEXT`), which leaves the change to the types alone. Prisma's enum form casts twice (`::text::"E_new"`).
.decl ctc_using(a: node)
ctc_using(a) :- ctc_using_expr(a, _), !ctc_plain_using(a).
.decl ctc_using_expr(a: node, e: node)
ctc_using_expr(a, e) :- kind(a, "alter_column"), child(a, k, i), kind(k, "keyword_using"), child(a, e, i + 1).
.decl ctc_unparen(e: node, x: node)
ctc_unparen(e, e) :- ctc_using_expr(_, e), !kind(e, "parenthesized_expression").
ctc_unparen(e, x) :- ctc_using_expr(_, e), kind(e, "parenthesized_expression"), child(e, c, 0), ctc_unparen2(c, x).
.decl ctc_unparen2(c: node, x: node)
ctc_unparen2(c, c) :- child(p, c, 0), kind(p, "parenthesized_expression"), !kind(c, "parenthesized_expression").
.decl ctc_plain_using(a: node)
ctc_plain_using(a) :- ctc_using_expr(a, e), ctc_unparen(e, f), ctc_is_col(a, f).
ctc_plain_using(a) :- ctc_using_expr(a, e), ctc_unparen(e, c), kind(c, "cast"), child(c, f, 0), ctc_is_col(a, f).
.decl ctc_is_col(a: node, f: node)  // f names a's own column
ctc_is_col(a, f) :- ctc_alter(a, _, _, x), kind(f, "field"), field(f, "name", n), pgm_ident(n, x).
// ctc_old(a, od): od is the latest definition of a's column before a, with no DROP COLUMN or RENAME COLUMN of that
// name between them (a column dropped and re-added, or renamed into place, has a type the rule does not follow).
.decl ctc_later(a: node, b: node)
ctc_later(a, b) :- ctc_before(a, b), ctc_before(a, c), ctc_pos(b, r, mb, ob), ctc_pos(c, r, mc, oc),
    (mb < mc ; mb = mc, ob < oc).
.decl ctc_reset(r: node, t: symbol, x: symbol)
ctc_reset(r, t, x) :- (kind(r, "drop_column") ; kind(r, "rename_column")), child(s, r, _), kind(s, "alter_table"),
    pgm_target(s, t), child(r, n, _), kind(n, "identifier"), pgm_ident(n, x).
.decl ctc_cut(a: node, b: node)
ctc_cut(a, b) :- ctc_before(a, b), ctc_alter(a, _, t, x), ctc_reset(r, t, x), ctc_pos(a, g, ma, oa),
    ctc_pos(b, g, mb, ob), ctc_pos(r, g, mr, orr), (mb < mr ; mb = mr, ob < orr), (mr < ma ; mr = ma, orr < oa).
.decl ctc_old(a: node, od: node)
ctc_old(a, b) :- ctc_before(a, b), !ctc_later(a, b), !ctc_cut(a, b).

// ---- types ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ctc_ty(p, base, p1, p2, arr): the type p gives: base name, its first and second modifier (-1 when absent), 1 when
// an array. INTEGER and INT are int, DECIMAL is numeric, CHARACTER VARYING is varchar, an enum or domain is "enum:Name"
// (CITEXT, which the grammar reads as a user type, is citext).
.decl ctc_ty(p: node, base: symbol, p1: number, p2: number, arr: number)
ctc_ty(p, b, p1, p2, ar) :- ctc_def(p, _, _), field(p, "type", y), ctc_ty_node(y), ctc_base(y, b), ctc_mod(y, 0, p1),
    ctc_mod(y, 1, p2), ctc_arr(p, ar).
ctc_ty(p, b, -1, -1, ar) :- ctc_def(p, _, _), field(p, "custom_type", o), field(o, "name", n), pgm_ident(n, x),
    (x = "citext", b = x ; x != "citext", b = cat("enum:", x)), ctc_arr(p, ar).
// ctc_base(y, b): type node y's base name: its text before any `(`, lower-cased, synonyms merged.
.decl ctc_base(y: node, b: symbol)
ctc_base(y, b) :- ctc_word(y, w), ctc_syn(w, b).
ctc_base(y, w) :- ctc_word(y, w), !ctc_syn(w, _).
.decl ctc_word(y: node, w: symbol)
ctc_word(y, @lower(W)) :- ctc_ty_node(y), text(y, s), match("\\s*(?<W>[^(]*[^( ])\\s*(\\(.*)?", s).
.decl ctc_syn(w: symbol, b: symbol)
ctc_syn("integer", "int"). ctc_syn("int4", "int"). ctc_syn("int8", "bigint"). ctc_syn("int2", "smallint").
ctc_syn("decimal", "numeric"). ctc_syn("character varying", "varchar"). ctc_syn("float8", "double precision").
ctc_syn("timestamp with time zone", "timestamptz"). ctc_syn("timestamp without time zone", "timestamp").
ctc_syn("bool", "boolean"). ctc_syn("float4", "real").
.decl ctc_mod(y: node, i: number, v: number)
ctc_mod(y, i, to_number(s)) :- ctc_ty_node(y), child(y, l, _), kind(l, "literal"), text(l, s),
    i = count : { child(y, l2, j), kind(l2, "literal"), child(y, l, k), j < k }.
ctc_mod(y, i, -1) :- ctc_ty_node(y), (i = 0 ; i = 1), count : { child(y, l, _), kind(l, "literal") } <= i.
.decl ctc_ty_node(y: node)
ctc_ty_node(y) :- ctc_def(p, _, _), field(p, "type", y), !kind(y, "array_size_definition").
.decl ctc_arr(p: node, ar: number)
ctc_arr(p, 1) :- ctc_def(p, _, _), child(p, c, _), kind(c, "array_size_definition").
ctc_arr(p, 0) :- ctc_def(p, _, _), count : { child(p, c, _), kind(c, "array_size_definition") } = 0.
// ctc_desc(p, s): the type as the message names it, from the source text: VARCHAR(100), "State", INTEGER[].
.decl ctc_desc(p: node, s: symbol)
ctc_desc(p, s) :- ctc_def(p, _, _), field(p, "type", y), !kind(y, "array_size_definition"), text(y, v), ctc_arr(p, ar),
    (ar = 1, s = cat(v, "[]") ; ar = 0, s = v).
ctc_desc(p, s) :- ctc_def(p, _, _), field(p, "custom_type", o), text(o, v), ctc_arr(p, ar),
    (ar = 1, s = cat(v, "[]") ; ar = 0, s = v).

// ---- which changes rewrite --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ctc_safe(od, a): from od's type to a's is binary coercible with a check PostgreSQL skips: the same type, a wider or
// removed length or precision, VARCHAR to TEXT, TIMESTAMP to TIMESTAMPTZ and back (see above).
.decl ctc_widen(b: symbol)  // types whose length or precision may grow or go without a rewrite
ctc_widen("varchar"). ctc_widen("numeric"). ctc_widen("timestamp"). ctc_widen("timestamptz"). ctc_widen("time").
ctc_widen("interval"). ctc_widen("varbit"). ctc_widen("bit_varying").
.decl ctc_safe(od: node, a: node)
ctc_safe(od, a) :- ctc_old(a, od), ctc_ty(od, b, p1, p2, ar), ctc_ty(a, b, p1, p2, ar).
ctc_safe(od, a) :- ctc_old(a, od), ctc_ty(od, b, _, _, ar), ctc_ty(a, b, -1, _, ar), ctc_widen(b).
ctc_safe(od, a) :- ctc_old(a, od), ctc_ty(od, b, p1, p2, ar), ctc_ty(a, b, q1, p2, ar), ctc_widen(b), p1 >= 0, q1 >= p1.
ctc_safe(od, a) :- ctc_old(a, od), ctc_ty(od, "varchar", _, _, ar), ctc_ty(a, "text", _, _, ar).
ctc_safe(od, a) :- ctc_old(a, od), ctc_ty(od, b, _, _, ar), ctc_ty(a, c, _, _, ar), ctc_citext(b, c).
.decl ctc_citext(b: symbol, c: symbol)  // binary casts the citext extension declares
ctc_citext("text", "citext"). ctc_citext("varchar", "citext"). ctc_citext("citext", "text").
ctc_safe(od, a) :- ctc_old(a, od), ctc_ty(od, "timestamp", _, _, ar), ctc_ty(a, "timestamptz", _, _, ar).
ctc_safe(od, a) :- ctc_old(a, od), ctc_ty(od, "timestamptz", _, _, ar), ctc_ty(a, "timestamp", _, _, ar).
// ctc_rewrites(a, od): a's change from od's type rewrites the table: a USING clause, or a change that is not safe.
// A type the rule cannot read on either side is not judged.
.decl ctc_rewrites(a: node, od: node)
ctc_rewrites(a, od) :- ctc_old(a, od), ctc_using(a).
ctc_rewrites(a, od) :- ctc_old(a, od), ctc_ty(od, _, _, _, _), ctc_ty(a, _, _, _, _), !ctc_safe(od, a).

// The cases, `cases/postgres-migrations-practice-column-type-change-rewrites/`, read as one repository: each line
// ending in `-- caught` is reported, and no other line. `cases/_git/` is a one-commit repository written as `.git`,
// so git_rev reads instead of withholding the rule; `.given pgm_applied` with no rows makes every case migration
// pending (a run with no base would read only each directory's newest).
.fixtures repo
    .fixture ".git/HEAD" from "../cases/_git/HEAD"
    .fixture ".git/config" from "../cases/_git/config"
    .fixture ".git/refs/heads/main" from "../cases/_git/refs/heads/main"
    .fixture ".git/objects/32/b988bd0a8e4bd9c69256baecd681a7eb9f1e53" from "../cases/_git/objects/32/b988bd0a8e4bd9c69256baecd681a7eb9f1e53"
    .fixture ".git/objects/4b/825dc642cb6eb9a060e54bf8d69288fbee4904" from "../cases/_git/objects/4b/825dc642cb6eb9a060e54bf8d69288fbee4904"
.end

.test cases exactly uses repo
    .given pgm_applied
    .fixture "drizzle/0000_init.sql" from "../cases/postgres-migrations-practice-column-type-change-rewrites/drizzle/0000_init.sql"
    .fixture "drizzle/0001_totals.sql" from "../cases/postgres-migrations-practice-column-type-change-rewrites/drizzle/0001_totals.sql"
    .fixture "prisma/migrations/20240101000000_init/migration.sql" from "../cases/postgres-migrations-practice-column-type-change-rewrites/prisma/migrations/20240101000000_init/migration.sql"
    .fixture "prisma/migrations/20240301000000_widen/migration.sql" from "../cases/postgres-migrations-practice-column-type-change-rewrites/prisma/migrations/20240301000000_widen/migration.sql"
    .fixture "prisma/migrations/20240401000000_bigint/migration.sql" from "../cases/postgres-migrations-practice-column-type-change-rewrites/prisma/migrations/20240401000000_bigint/migration.sql"
    .fixture "prisma/migrations/20240501000000_audit_log/migration.sql" from "../cases/postgres-migrations-practice-column-type-change-rewrites/prisma/migrations/20240501000000_audit_log/migration.sql"
    .fixture "prisma/migrations/20240701000000_swap_names/migration.sql" from "../cases/postgres-migrations-practice-column-type-change-rewrites/prisma/migrations/20240701000000_swap_names/migration.sql"
    .fixture "prisma/migrations/20240801000000_timestamps_back/migration.sql" from "../cases/postgres-migrations-practice-column-type-change-rewrites/prisma/migrations/20240801000000_timestamps_back/migration.sql"
    .fixture "prisma/migrations/migration_lock.toml" from "../cases/postgres-migrations-practice-column-type-change-rewrites/prisma/migrations/migration_lock.toml"
    .expect _ at "drizzle/0001_totals.sql":1
    .expect _ at "prisma/migrations/20240401000000_bigint/migration.sql":2
    .expect _ at "prisma/migrations/20240401000000_bigint/migration.sql":3
    .expect _ at "prisma/migrations/20240401000000_bigint/migration.sql":4
    .expect _ at "prisma/migrations/20240401000000_bigint/migration.sql":5
    .expect _ at "prisma/migrations/20240401000000_bigint/migration.sql":11
.end
